            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "विशेषज्ञः — viśeṣajñaḥ — \"an expert\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "रोगस्य विषये विशेषज्ञं पृच्छतु। rogasya viṣaye viśeṣajñaṃ pṛcchatu. Ask an expert about the illness."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A masculine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "विशेषज्ञः (viśeṣajñaḥ) is built from viśeṣa, \"a distinction\", and jña, \"knowing\"; MW gives viśeṣa-jña \"knowing distinctions, judicious\", and \"an expert\" is its modern sense (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
